AB  - Based on prescreening results, a strain of Beauveria sp. Ba02 having monoamine oxidase inhibitary activity was selected for further liquid fermentation. The fermentation broth was extracted with different solvents, and the results revealed that acylacetate was the best solvent for MAO inhibitor extraction. By means of bioactive guided isolation of column chromatography and preparative high performance chromatography, a deep red pure compound was obtained. The inhibition rates of the compound on MAO-A and B are 97.50% and 95.34% respectively at the concentration of 15 Mu-g.mL~(-1). By the methods of MS and NMR the compound was identified as oosporein. Although the compound is a known one, its MAO inhibition activities were revealed for the first time.
